 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242731,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/74a2b08a46329e37.jpg\" alt=\"A table with the first column headed “Calls made by small bird.” Mobbing call has a call sound frequency of 4.5 kHz, small bird hearing range (1–10 kHz) “yes,” and large bird hearing range (1–4 kHz) “yes.” Scolding call has a call sound frequency of 4 kHz, small bird hearing range (1–10 kHz) “yes,” and large bird hearing range (1–4 kHz) “yes.” Warning call has a call sound frequency of 7–8 kHz, small bird hearing range (1–10 kHz) “yes,” and large bird hearing range (1–4 kHz) “no.”\"></p>\n<p>A small bird makes three different kinds of calls: A mobbing call that a group of adults make when mobbing a single predator bird in defense of their nests, a scolding call that a single bird makes to disturb a predator bird perched nearby, and a warning call that a single bird makes to warn other birds when a predator bird flies into the vicinity.</p>\n<p>A study analyzed the sound frequencies of different calls. The table summarizes the findings.</p>\n<p>Based on this information, make a claim about the calls the small bird makes. (credit: Behavioral Ecology and Sociobiology)</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760385,
     "content_html": "A scolding call cannot be heard by other small birds. This is because the scolding call targets a larger bird. There is no advantage in other small birds hearing it."
    },
    {
     "id": 760384,
     "content_html": "The mobbing can be heard by large predator birds. Therefore small birds cannot defend their nests without the predators knowing. This is an unfavorable trait and is naturally selected."
    },
    {
     "id": 760383,
     "content_html": "The scolding call cannot be heard by large birds. Therefore, the scolding call is not effective in its purpose. This is an unfavorable trait, but the small birds still has it."
    },
    {
     "id": 760386,
     "content_html": "The warning call cannot be heard by large predator birds. This gives the small birds an advanced warning. This is a favorable trait that gives birds a survival advantage."
    }
   ],
